From 69f8df8e87118ad99ed8162bf0a5ba64e8397dfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shine5402 <14089306+shine5402@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:47:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Allow disabling Blink scheduler throttling per RenderView

Ported from Electron's patches/chromium/allow_disabling_blink_scheduler_throttling_per_renderview.patch
(originally by deepak1556), which Electron uses for its webPreferences
backgroundThrottling option.

Add PageBroadcast.SetSchedulerThrottling(bool), sent through
RenderViewHost::SetSchedulerThrottling. While throttling is disallowed,
WebViewImpl reports every visibility the browser sends as kVisible, so
the page, its scheduler and everything observing its visibility treat a
hidden page as a shown one. The browser's own visibility is remembered
and re-applied when throttling is allowed again.

Electron's change to RenderWidgetHostViewAura::ShowImpl is left out: Qt
WebEngine does not use that view. The default, throttling allowed,
leaves Chromium's behavior unchanged.
